1️⃣ Check if a Number is a Power of 2
👉 Concept

A number is a power of 2 if it has only ONE set bit (1) in binary.
Example:

8 → 1000 ✅

10 → 1010 ❌

👉 Logic
n & (n - 1) == 0   → power of 2

👉 Code
public class PowerOfTwo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 8;

        if (n > 0 && (n & (n - 1)) == 0) {
            System.out.println("Power of 2");
        } else {
            System.out.println("Not a power of 2");
        }
    }
}

2️⃣ Toggle a Bit at Position pos in Number n
👉 Concept

Toggle means:

1 → 0

0 → 1

👉 Logic
Toggle → XOR (^)
n ^ (1 << pos)

👉 Code
public class ToggleBit {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 5;    // 0101
        int pos = 1;

        int result = n ^ (1 << pos);
        System.out.println(result);
    }
}

3️⃣ Count Number of 1’s in Binary Representation
👉 Concept

Count how many 1s are present in the binary form of a number.

👉 Efficient Logic (Brian Kernighan’s Algorithm)

Each step removes the rightmost set bit.

n = n & (n - 1)

👉 Code
public class CountOnes {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 13; // 1101
        int count = 0;

        while (n != 0) {
            n = n & (n - 1);
            count++;
        }

        System.out.println(count);
    }
}

4️⃣ Decimal to Binary Conversion
👉 Concept

Divide number by 2

Store remainders

Read in reverse order

👉 Code
public class DecimalToBinary {
    static void decimalToBinary(int n) {
        String binary = "";

        while (n > 0) {
            binary = (n % 2) + binary;
            n = n / 2;
        }

        System.out.println(binary);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        decimalToBinary(10);
    }
}

5️⃣ Binary to Decimal Conversion
👉 Concept

Multiply each digit by powers of 2.

👉 Code
public class BinaryToDecimal {
    static void binaryToDecimal(String binary) {
        int decimal = 0;
        int power = 0;

        for (int i = binary.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            int digit = binary.charAt(i) - '0';
            decimal += digit * Math.pow(2, power);
            power++;
        }

        System.out.println(decimal);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        binaryToDecimal("1010");
    }
}

🔑 One-Line Summary
Power of 2 → n & (n - 1) == 0
Toggle Bit → n ^ (1 << pos)
Count 1s   → n = n & (n - 1)
Dec → Bin  → divide by 2
Bin → Dec  → sum of (digit × 2^position)
